# What a proficiency is worth. AUTO:WEAPONPROF and CSKILL record that a
# character is proficient; they compute nothing. These attach the
# proficiency bonus to each save, weapon type and skill, and define the
# bonus itself. Without them a character sheet prints +0 for everything.
#
# Also here, for the same reason -- machinery rather than content, hung
# off the one ability every character has:
#   the pools a player spends, declared so a category's POOL: always
#   names a variable that exists;
#   the languages, one selectable ability apiece, plus the Common every
#   character knows;
#   the one spell slot table a character has, however many classes cast;
#   and what wearing armour untrained costs, which the equipment attaches.

Default	CATEGORY:Internal	DEFINE:Proficiency_Bonus|0	BONUS:VAR|Proficiency_Bonus|(TL+7)/4|TYPE=Base|!PRERACE:1,TYPE=Monster	DEFINE:POOL_Origin_Feat|0	DEFINE:POOL_General_Feat|0	DEFINE:POOL_Fighting_Style_Feat|0	DEFINE:POOL_Epic_Boon_Feat|0	DEFINE:POOL_Background|0	DEFINE:POOL_Language_Selection|0	DEFINE:POOL_Expertise|0	AUTO:LANG|Common	BONUS:VAR|POOL_Language_Selection|2	BONUS:VAR|POOL_Background|1	ABILITY:SkillExport|AUTOMATIC|TYPE=SkillExport	DEFINE:DarkvisionRange|0	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Darkvision|PREVARGTEQ:DarkvisionRange,1	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Spellcaster Spell Slots	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|First Level Proficiencies|PREPCLEVEL:MIN=1
